COMMENT     PROVISIONAL REFSEQ: This record has not yet been subject to final
            NCBI review. The reference sequence was derived from X83413.
            
            [WARNING] On Nov 14, 2017 this sequence was replaced by
            NC_001664.3.
            
            On Feb 24, 2009 this sequence version replaced NC_001664.1.
            ACCURACY: Potential frameshifts in DR6.
            REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by Dr. Andrew Davison
            (MRC-University of Glasgow Centre for Virus Research, Glasgow, UK).
            The reference sequence was derived from X83413.
            CURATION: The original gene nomenclature has been retained. Genes
            presumably inherited from the common ancestor of alpha-, beta- and
            gammaherpesviruses (core genes), from the common ancestor of beta-
            and gammaherpesviruses (betagamma genes), from the common ancestor
            of betaherpesviruses (beta genes) are indicated. Initiation codons
            are assigned with as much confidence as is possible for each
            protein-coding region. A standard protein nomenclature has been
            applied so that orthologs have the same name in all herpesviruses.
            Protein information may have been propagated from other herpesvirus
            species.
            COMPLETENESS: full length.
