            quality control of annotation results performed by Jordan Moberg
            Parker and Dallas Mould (UCLA). Assembly confirmed by Charles
            Bowman (University of Pittsburgh). Sequencing by 454 to
            approximately 122x coverage performed at The UCLA Genotyping and
            Sequencing Core, Los Angeles, CA. Assembly performed with Newbler
            and Consed software as of September 2014, producing a complete
            genome sequence having defined physical ends with 11 base 3' single
            strand overhang (TCGTACGGCTT) and 54.2% GC content. Project
            supported at UCLA, in part, as member institution of the Howard
            Hughes Medical Institute Science Education Alliance (SEA-PHAGES).
            
